# Qualitative data for the logistic model, in PyBNF's Biological Property
# Specification Language (BPSL). Each line is a constraint the trajectory must
# satisfy; a fit is penalized by how much it violates them (0 = all satisfied).
#
# Syntax:  <expr> <op> <expr>  <where>  [weight <w>]
#   <where>:  at <indvar>=<value>   -- at one point
#             always                -- at every output point
#             once                  -- at least once
#             between a=<v1>,a=<v2> -- over an interval
#
# These four encode what we qualitatively "know" about the population, without
# any numeric measurements:

# It starts small.
Obs_N < 10 at time=0

# It has passed the inflection (half of carrying capacity) by mid-run.
Obs_N > 50 at time=4

# It has essentially reached capacity by the end.
Obs_N > 90 at time=8

# It never overshoots its carrying capacity.
Obs_N < 105 always
